    "title": "William Shatner Was 'Slow Moving' in Recent Public Outing After 'Being Driven' to Event - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Michael Gioia ,\n5 hours ago Eric Kowalsky / MEGA William Shatner was taking his time over the weekend.\nThe Canadian actor, best known for playing Captain James T. Kirk in the Star Trek film franchise, stepped out on Saturday, May 30, in California to meet some of his fans .\nAlongside other celebs that included Heather Locklear , Lorenzo Lamas , Priscilla Presley and Engelbert Humperdinck , Shatner attended The Hollywood Show at the Los Angeles Marriott Burbank Airport Hotel, where fans could take selfies and ask for autographs.\nA source exclusively tells Closer that the 95-year-old was “ slow moving as he walked ” into the event.\nColeman-Rayner “It’s the first time I have seen him being driven to an event ,” the eyewitness says. “In the past, he has always driven himself to all events and dinners.”\nStill, when it comes to his career, Shatner hasn’t seemed to slow down at all . The Boston Legal alum is hard at work making multiple appearances across the United States.\nAccording to his tour website , Shatner “takes the stage to share fascinating and humorous behind-the-scenes stories from his life and illustrious career, including answering audience questions.”\nAside from Shatner’s solo engagements, the actor has also made recent appearances alongside astrophysicist and writer Neil deGrasse Tyson .\nEarlier this year, Shatner slammed fake posts claiming that he’s dying.\nColeman-Rayner “There is a page on @facebook that is using AI to create horrible fake news stories about me. The page is by The Beanstalk Functions Group which is allegedly an Event Planner in South Africa,” he wrote on X . “They have created stories that say I have stage 4 brain cancer, was in some kind of fight with Erika Kirk and that I’m dying.”\nExplaining that the stories are allegedly “monetized,” Shatner said, “None of these stories are true but they apparently seem genuine enough for fans to repost them across social media and send messages of support to me and my family all while the culprits behind the account make money.”\n“This is the downside of AI and yellow journalism,” he added.\nRead More From Closer Weekly 5",
    "summary": "5 hours ago Eric Kowalsky / MEGA William Shatner was taking his time over the weekend. The Canadian actor, best known for playing Captain James T. Kirk in the Star Trek film franchise, stepped out on Saturday, May 30, in California to meet some of his fans . Alongside other celebs that included Heather Locklear , Lorenzo Lamas , Priscilla Presley and Engelbert Humperdinck , Shatner attended The Hollywood Show at the Los Angeles Marriott Burbank Airport Hotel, where fans could take selfies and ask for autographs.",
